---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { useTranslations, type Lang } from "../../i18n/ui";

const lang: Lang = "en";
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout title={`${t("datenschutz.title")} | Playground`}>
  <section class="pg-section">
    <div class="pg-prose">
      <p class="pg-eyebrow">{t("datenschutz.eyebrow")}</p>
      <h1>{t("datenschutz.title")}</h1>

      <p>
        The protection of your personal data is important to us. This website can generally be used without providing personal data. To the extent that personal data is processed on this website, it is done in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and applicable data protection laws.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>
        The controller responsible under the GDPR is:<br />
        <strong>Please replace this with your own data:</strong><br />
        Your name/company name<br />
        Street address and house number<br />
        Postal code and city<br />
        Phone: +49 123 456789<br />
        Email: contact@example.com
      </p>

      <h2>2. Server Log Files</h2>
      <p>
        Whenever you access this website, our hosting provider (Cloudflare) automatically collects general data and information (e.g., browser type, operating system used, referrer URL, pages visited, date and time of access). This data is stored in log files and does not allow direct conclusions about your person. Processing is based on Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR (legitimate interest in system security).
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses cookies. Technically necessary cookies are required for the website to function and are set without separate consent. Additionally, we set analytics cookies — <strong>only with your explicit consent</strong> — to improve your experience of the website.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can adjust or withdraw your consent at any time via the cookie banner or the "Cookie settings" link in the footer.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Google Analytics via Google Tag Manager</h2>
      <p>
        If you have consented, we integrate the Google Analytics web analytics service via Google Tag Manager. The provider is Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland ("Google").
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Analytics uses cookies and technologies that enable an analysis of your use of this website (e.g., pages visited, time spent, approximate location, technical device information). This data is transmitted encrypted to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        This processing is based solely on your consent (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. a GDPR), which you provide via the cookie banner. <strong>Before your consent, no analytics cookies are set and no data is transferred to Google</strong> — this is technically implemented by the "Google Consent Mode," which blocks data collection.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your personal data may also be transferred to Google LLC in the United States. Google LLC is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; additionally, EU Standard Contractual Clauses serve as a guarantee for an adequate level of data protection (Art. 46 GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        For more information about Google Analytics, visit: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </p>

      <h2>5. YouTube Videos</h2>
      <p>
        This website contains embedded YouTube videos in Enhanced Privacy Mode from youtube-nocookie.com. This means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cookies:</strong> No cookie is set without you actively watching a video</li>
        <li><strong>No tracking data:</strong> YouTube does not collect user data from viewers who do not actively play a video</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy by default:</strong> This embedding method respects your privacy</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you play a video, YouTube and Google may collect data about your viewing behavior. This is subject to the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us via email, contact form, or other channels, the data you provide (e.g., name, email address, message text) will be processed solely for the purpose of responding to your inquiry and will not be shared with third parties without your consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Processing is based on Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR (performance of a contract) or Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR (legitimate interest).
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        As a data subject, you have the following rights under the GDPR:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to access</strong> (Art. 15 GDPR): You can request access to the personal data we process about you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to rectification</strong> (Art. 16 GDPR): You can have incorrect data corrected.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to erasure</strong> (Art. 17 GDPR): Under certain circumstances, you can request the deletion of your data ("right to be forgotten").
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to restrict processing</strong> (Art. 18 GDPR): You can request restriction of processing your data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to data portability</strong> (Art. 20 GDPR): You can receive your data in a structured form and transfer it to another provider.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to object</strong> (Art. 21 GDPR): You can object to the processing of your data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> (Art. 7 para. 3 GDPR): You can withdraw any given consent at any time with future effect.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to lodge a complaint</strong> (Art. 77 GDPR): You have the right to file a complaint with a data protection authority.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses SSL/TLS encryption for the transmission of confidential content. You can identify an encrypted connection by "https://" in your browser's address bar and a lock icon.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this privacy policy as soon as legal requirements or website functions change. The currently published version on this page applies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
